# Never upload the Python virtualenv.
#
# It is ~900MB of nothing the site needs, and it contains venv/bin/python — a
# symlink pointing outside the project root. Turbopack walked into it while
# resolving @ffmpeg-installer's computed require and the build died with
# "Symlink venv/bin/python is invalid, it points out of the filesystem root",
# blaming the route that triggered the walk rather than the symlink.
#
# Excluding it here fixes the upload cost and removes the landmine for whatever
# resolves a directory next.
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local scratch that has no business in a deployment.
experiments/

# The Video Cutter is a LOCAL tool and was never meant to ship.
#
# The deploy rejected it at 307.94MB against a 250MB limit — the same number as
# a previous rejection, which is the tell that nothing had actually changed.
# Removing its outputFileTracingIncludes entry did not help, because nothing was
# including ffmpeg by configuration: the route locates the binary with
# join(process.cwd(), "node_modules", "@ffmpeg-installer", ...) and Turbopack
# resolves that computed path as a directory reference and traces what it finds.
# Same mechanism as the venv symlink above.
#
# Excluding the binary from tracing would have worked and would have been the
# wrong fix. On the hosted function ffmpegAvailable() already returns false, the
# upload caps near 100MB and the run at 300s — it could never cut real footage
# there. So it does not deploy at all. It still runs locally, and
# scripts/video_assemble.js is the pipeline that actually renders.
app/admin/video-editor/
app/api/admin/video-editor/
